-- ============================================================================
--  0049 · Seed the lab test master with the reference-lab rate list
-- ============================================================================
--  525 single tests from the lab's rate list -- name, method, sample,
--  volume, scheduled days, cut-off time, reporting time, the patient rate and
--  the lab rate -- so lab users can pick them when they build a Group Test or
--  Package on the console's Lab Tests > Test Master tab, and edit any of them.
--
--  * Patient rate goes to rate / amount (no discount); lab rate to lab_rate.
--    A dash or blank in the list is stored as empty text or 0 ("not quoted").
--  * Department is not in the list, so it is left blank for the lab to fill in.
--  * Typos in the reporting-time column were tidied ("3rdDay" -> "3rd Day",
--    "3thDay" -> "3rd Day", "3r Day" -> "3rd Day", "7rd Day" -> "7th Day",
--    "10 Days" -> "10th Day", "One week" -> "1 week"). Anything else, such as
--    Platelet Antibodies' "Wed", is kept as the list has it.
--  * Immunohistochemistry has no rate in the list ("Please contact for more
--    details"); that text is kept as its internal note. Adrenaline
--    (Epinephrine) has no details at all, so only its name is stored.
--
--  Needs 0046 (the lab_test tables) and 0048 (scheduled_days, reporting_time,
--  lab_rate) applied first. Idempotent and safe to re-run: a test whose name
--  already exists (ignoring case) is skipped, never overwritten, so edits made
--  in the console survive. Lis Codes are handed out by the database.
--    dart run backend/db/apply_migration.dart backend/db/migrations/0049_seed_lab_test_rate_list.sql --yes
-- ============================================================================

SET search_path TO app, public;

